women's body sizes, women's travel patterns&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:04.680 --> 01:57:11.520
ends up costing society at large. I think it's an&nbsp;
excellent way of getting that. Then the other book&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:11.520 --> 01:57:15.120
that I love the most, it's a very grandiose&nbsp;
title. It's called The Dawn of Everything:&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:15.120 --> 01:57:20.940
A New History of Humanity by David Graeber.&nbsp;
I actually love everything that guy wrote.&nbsp;

01:57:20.940 --> 01:57:28.560
I started with this book called Bullshit Jobs,&nbsp;
which — I was dealing with the bureaucracy of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:28.560 --> 01:57:34.680
academia and feeling very frustrated. I read&nbsp;
that book and it was very cathartic, and then&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:34.680 --> 01:57:39.720
I just went down the rabbit hole and have enjoyed&nbsp;
all the other books. But The Dawn of Everything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:40.740 --> 01:57:47.880
it's a big book and it's pretty thick, but the&nbsp;
last chapter has some really cool stuff about&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:47.880 --> 01:57:58.800
